<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:30:54Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Will Germany have enough gas this winter amid energy supply crunch?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d009614f7bfd9aa9f0c9269cd62ed13c03880d02b9d62986927527cf06fda9b0</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:30:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T08:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-germany-have-enough-gas-this-winter-amid-energy-supply-crunch/a-79360317--cfd94c55c93d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-germany-have-enough-gas-this-winter-amid-energy-supply-crunch/a-79360317?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's gas storage sites are far less full than in recent years. Officials say supplies are secure, but analysts warn that a cold winter or import disruptions could push prices higher. So how secure is the supply?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: VW to step up cost-cutting program</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02d80d634c2b63d0701a3e62fea49ceb9d95fdfe45244b9d8ab3700c54ffa5d6</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:30:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T07:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-vw-to-step-up-cost-cutting-program/live-79365190--a755a3e03dbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-vw-to-step-up-cost-cutting-program/live-79365190?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Volkswagen's chief says the carmaker will accelerate its streamlining measures as workers protest. The Israeli ambassador says the Left Party win in Berlin polls poses a risk to the city's Jewish community. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Trial starts of ex-Transport Minister Scheuer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08d04729187c6a56a4c6619bd5f0b81e189f1dfc402b6d92bfc27a2eb56316b5</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-trial-starts-of-ex-transport-minister-scheuer/live-79351160--5052118e7b45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-trial-starts-of-ex-transport-minister-scheuer/live-79351160?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former Transport Minister Andreas Scheuer is being tried for perjury related to a failed car toll scheme. And cherry farmers have brought in a bumper harvest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Chancellor Merz braces for difficult days ahead</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e2d1cb9f158ce4ff730d08be96f57834691d7c3cb15b874ddcb04156742131f</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:30:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T07:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-chancellor-merz-braces-for-difficult-days-ahead/a-79365325--7a0c9fa42acf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-chancellor-merz-braces-for-difficult-days-ahead/a-79365325?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's far-right AfD and the socialist Left Party gained ground in recent state elections, while the centrist parties lost support. The biggest loser is Chancellor Friedrich Merz.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's car crisis: Can the 35-hour workweek survive?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abeecb7bdc39b1ed3c94ae8cfa7f768991b06cf1fad4495289f8b894652a963c</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-car-crisis-can-the-35-hour-workweek-survive/a-79307488--cb2e3220b33e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-car-crisis-can-the-35-hour-workweek-survive/a-79307488?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German carmakers want employees to work 40 hours instead of the current 35 without extra pay, arguing it would improve competitiveness. Unions strongly oppose the proposal and view it as an attack on workers' rights.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>German state elections deal a blow to Chancellor Friedrich Merz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:289145345278a095da2a455542ceaa57b06cb9eae25d98eb2906aac1743e7bac</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T21:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-state-elections-deal-a-blow-to-chancellor-friedrich-merz/a-79348585--45dd8fc79779.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-state-elections-deal-a-blow-to-chancellor-friedrich-merz/a-79348585?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Elections in Berlin and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania have dealt the CDU a historic defeat while the AfD saw a massive gain. The pressure on Germany's unpopular chancellor is mounting.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Oktoberfest 2026: Everything you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cbccf9af32cdf63c9de6475900a5f472f85406f291fd41048d07be45ce9b4c0</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285--1e3ee9d16248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285?maca=en-rss-en-ger-102